cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  methodological paper listed under references.
title: starfold
abstract: >-
  Starfold finds groups in a numeric table without labels and measures how
  far they can be trusted. It searches UMAP and HDBSCAN settings with
  Optuna, scores each setting without labels against structureless copies
  of the table, refits the selected setting on random subsets to measure
  how often each row and group recurs, and offers an optional Monte Carlo
  calibration test. It extends the method of Neitzel et al. (2025).
type: software
